        "notes": "Detached (own group) only when --timeout is given; a normal run is unchanged except for the signal handling. Group ids are removed on close and on timeout so a finished run's group is not signalled again; the leader's pid is still signalled once on its exit, after it was reaped, which leaves a tiny pid-reuse window (in TODO). The failing run reports 'timed out after N min'. Parse accepts a plain positive decimal up to a week; Windows is refused in review.ts before any workspace. On the leader exiting, its group is killed so a leftover background process cannot hold the run open; a finished review is kept. On timeout, partial output goes to the log, not the output. A reviewer that calls setsid escapes. SIGHUP and SIGQUIT are handled like SIGINT/SIGTERM (exit codes 129/131) so the exit handler runs when the terminal closes. Partial output is cleaned (cleanText) and cut to its last 3000 characters so the header survives the 4000-character cut in the failure block. Overlap: hunk h6 line 4 (the shared usage line) is listed here and in evidence-stage, since both add a flag to it. SIGHUP/SIGQUIT handling applies to ALL runs, timed or not: untimed runs now dispose their workspaces and exit 129/131 where before SIGHUP just killed git-gud and SIGQUIT dumped core. After a timeout or the 2 s fallback git-gud destroys the reviewer's pipes and unrefs it, so it exits even if a process that escaped the group holds them."
